From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:56:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommbe: ipq95xx: c-460: leave the QCN9074 radio off

The C-460's QCN9074 on pcie0 stops answering at its first interface on
every public firmware tried so far (B175 in the port's records). "wifi
config" still adds its radio enabled, keeping the world domain, and
every Wi-Fi reload then flips the regulatory domain of the other three
radios (B180). Disable that radio when it is first added; a disabled
option already set is kept.

A port patch until the radio works; not for upstream.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 .../ieee80211/13-arista-c-460-scan-radio      | 31 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)
 create mode 100755 target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/13-arista-c-460-scan-radio

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/13-arista-c-460-scan-radio b/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/13-arista-c-460-scan-radio
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..3c7ea2f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/13-arista-c-460-scan-radio
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Arista C-460: the QCN9074 on pcie0 does not run yet on any public
+# firmware (it stops answering at its first interface). Leave its radio
+# disabled when "wifi config" first adds it: an enabled radio without a
+# country of its own keeps the world domain ('00') and flips the
+# regulatory domain of the other radios on every reload. A disabled
+# option already set, either way, is left alone.
+
+[ "$ACTION" = add ] || exit 0
+
+. /lib/functions.sh
+
+[ "$(board_name)" = arista,c-460 ] || exit 0
+
+case "$(readlink "/sys/class/ieee80211/$DEVICENAME/device")" in
+*/0000:01:00.0)
+	;;
+*)
+	exit 0
+	;;
+esac
+
+for s in $(uci -q show wireless | sed -n 's/^wireless\.\([^.=]*\)=wifi-device$/\1/p'); do
+	case "$(uci -q get "wireless.$s.path")" in
+	*/0000:01:00.0)
+		uci -q get "wireless.$s.disabled" >/dev/null && exit 0
+		uci set "wireless.$s.disabled=1"
+		uci commit wireless
+		;;
+	esac
+done
